Separation of duties: Different roles have different capabilities
Scalability: Easy to add new roles, users, and permissions
Real-World Applications
RBAC is used in:

Operating systems: Linux file permissions, Windows Active Directory
Databases: PostgreSQL roles, MySQL user privileges
Cloud platforms: AWS IAM, Azure RBAC, Google Cloud IAM
Applications: Content management systems, enterprise software
Key Takeaways
RBAC simplifies permission management by grouping permissions into roles
Users inherit permissions from their assigned roles
One user can have multiple roles, combining their permissions
This model scales better than assigning individual permissions to users
